# Byte-for-byte is this repository's whole test strategy, so git must not
# rewrite a single byte on the way in or out.
#
# `doctor` compares every generated file against a fresh render byte for byte
# (§0.2, §10), and the script tests assert program output against goldens
# extracted from testdata/script/*.txtar with testscript's `cmp`, which is a
# byte comparison and applies no line-ending conversion of its own. Git for
# Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` by default: without this file, a checkout
# there rewrites every golden's LF to CRLF while the program still prints LF,
# and twenty-odd `cmp` assertions fail on line endings alone — a red suite that
# says nothing about para.
#
# `-text` on everything is the blunt version deliberately. Scoping it to the
# formats that matter today means the next format added is the next Windows
# failure, and there is no file in this repository that wants conversion.
* -text
